{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30153 - PROTEIN:4915",
  "verbalization": "Methyl Lucidenate Q appears to interact with the CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is a target of multiple compounds, including Leosibirone B and another metabolite. This enzyme is ultimately linked to Replicase polyprotein 1ab, suggesting a potential role in the replication of viral proteins. The evidence indicates that Methyl Lucidenate Q may act as a modulator of this enzyme, possibly through a metabolic pathway that involves the conversion of CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside into a different compound, which in turn targets Replicase polyprotein 1ab. The shared target of multiple compounds and the indirect pathway through the sialyltransferase suggest that Methyl Lucidenate Q may influence viral replication by affecting the enzymatic activity of this critical protein. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Methyl Lucidenate Q could exert its effects on viral replication, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism.",
